data: {""p"":""/message/content/parts/0"",""o"":""append"",""v"":""If your credit report shows **\u201cSuit Filed,\u201d""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" \u201cWilful Default,\u201d or \u201c""}  

event: delta
data: {""v"":""Written Off,\u201d** these are serious negative credit-report""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" entries in India. They can make getting loans or credit cards much harder.\n\n### What each term""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" means\n\n| Status | Meaning |\n|---|---|\n| **Suit Filed** | The lender has""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" reported that legal proceedings have been""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" initiated regarding the debt. |\n| **Wilful Default** | The lender has classified the borrower as a wilful defaulter under applicable RBI rules\u2014generally involving""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" deliberate non-payment despite the ability to pay, diversion/siph""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":""oning of funds, etc. |\n| **Written Off** | The""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" lender has treated the debt as an accounting loss. **It does not mean the debt has been legally forgiven.** |\n\n### Can you remove these from""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" your credit report?\n\n**If they're accurate:** You generally cannot simply ask Exper""}  

event: delta
data: {""v"":""ian/CIBIL to delete them.\n\n**If they're inaccurate:** You can dispute the information with the credit bureau and the lender. For""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" example, if:\n- You never had the account\n- The account belongs to someone else\n- The amount""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":""/status is wrong\n- The lender has reported a suit that was withdrawn/settled""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" but hasn't updated the report\n- You've already paid the debt but the status hasn't been""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" updated correctly\n\n### If the account is written off\n\nIf you still owe the lender, contact the lender and discuss""}  

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" repayment/settlement. **Be careful with \u201csettlement\u201d**: settling for less than the full amount""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" can itself be reported as **\u201csettled,\u201d** which is generally viewed negatively by lenders.\n\nIf possible, ask the""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" lender what is required for the account to be reported as **\u201cclosed\u201d** rather than merely \u201csettled.\u201d\n\n### If you have a wil""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":""ful-default classification\n\nThis is more serious than an ordinary late payment. Don't assume that paying the""}  

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" outstanding amount automatically removes the classification. You should obtain the lender's records and understand **why the""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" classification was made** and whether the underlying information is still accurate.\n\nIf you tell me **exactly what your Experian""}     

event: delta
data: {""v"":""/CIBIL report says** (for example, *\u201cWritten Off \u20b9X,\u201d \u201cSuit""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" Filed,\u201d or \u201cWilful Default\u201d*), I can explain **what you can do to correct it and improve your credit profile**""}  

