data: {""p"":""/message/content/parts/0"",""o"":""append"",""v"":""Yes \u2014 **absolutely.** You can pay your credit""}  

event: delta
data: {""v"":""-card bill **before the""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" due date**, and it's generally a good habit""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"". \ud83d\udc4d\n\n### Example\nSuppose:\n- Bill generated: **\u20b920,000**\n- Due date: **25 September""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":""**\n- You pay: **\u20b920,000 on 15 September**\n\n\u2705 Your bill is paid on time  \n\u2705 You""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" avoid late-payment charges/interest  \n\u2705 It helps maintain a good repayment history\n\n### Can""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" you pay before the bill is generated?\nYes. You can also make payments during the billing cycle""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":"". However, make sure you still check the **final statement**""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" and pay any remaining amount by the due date.\n\n### For improving your credit score\n""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":""Since you're currently around **770**, a good approach is:\n- Pay the **full statement amount""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":""**, not just the minimum due.\n- Pay before the due date.\n- Keep credit utilization relatively""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" low.\n- Avoid unnecessary credit-card/loan applications.\n\n**Tip:** Paying the full balance""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" every month is usually better than carrying a balance just to \""build credit.\"" You don't need to pay interest to build a good credit score""}    

event: delta
