data: {""p"":""/message/content/parts/0"",""o"":""append"",""v"":""A **credit-card billing cycle""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":""** is the period during""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" which your card purchases are accumulated into one statement. Understanding it""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" helps you avoid interest and late fees.\n\n""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":""### \ud83d\udd04 How the billing cycle works\n\nFor example""}     

event: delta
data: {""v"":"":\n\n- **Billing cycle:** 1st\u201330th of each month\n- **Statement date:** 30th\n- **Payment due date:** around 15th of""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" the following month\n\nIf you spend:\n\n| Date | Purchase | Amount |\n|---|---|""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":""---:|\n| May 5 | Groceries | \u20b95,000 |\n| May""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" 12 | Fuel | \u20b92,000 |\n| May 25 | Shopping | \u20b98,000 |\n| **Total** | | **\u20b915,000** |\n\n""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":""Your bank generates a statement for **\u20b915,000** on May 30. You then have until the **payment""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" due date** to pay it.\n\n### \ud83d\udca1 The important""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" terms\n\n**Statement date:** The day your bank closes the billing cycle and generates your bill.\n\n**Total amount due:** The full amount you owe for that statement""}   

event: delta
data: {""v"":"". **Paying this in full by the due date is generally the best approach.**\n\n**Minimum amount due:** The smallest amount you must pay to avoid being classified as late, but paying only""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" this can result in interest on the remaining balance.\n\n**Due date:** The deadline for""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" payment.\n\n### \ud83d\uddd3\ufe0f What happens after the statement""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":""?\n\nPurchases made **after the statement date** normally appear on your **next statement**.\n\nFor example, if your statement closes on May 30""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"":\n\n- \u20b910,000 spent on **May 29** \u2192 May statement\n- \u20b910,000 spent on **May 31** \u2192 June statement\n\nThis is why a purchase made just after""}

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" your statement date can potentially get a longer interest-free period, assuming you pay the statement balance in full and""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" your card terms provide an interest-free period.\n\n### \u2b50 For maintaining""} 

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" your 770 CIBIL score\n\nSince you mentioned your CIBIL score is **770**, focus on:\n\n**Use""}    

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" card \u2192 statement generated \u2192 pay the full statement amount before the due date.**\n\nYou **do not need to carry""}      

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" a balance or pay credit-card interest** to build a good credit score.\n\nIf you tell me your **card's statement date and payment""}       

event: delta
data: {""v"":"" due date**, I can show you exactly **which purchases will appear on each""}       

event: delta
